In Linear, priority: 0 = no priority, 1 = low, 2 = medium, 3 = high, 4 = urgent.

"High priority" → priority = 3 (High). "At risk" → probably project state name "At Risk". Linear's project states have names like "Planned", "Started", "Completed", "Paused", "Canceled". Custom states can also exist. "At risk" might be a state name that the organization has set up.

"Milestone deadline of December 2, 2026" — a project's milestone field, or a milestone project. Hmm, in Linear projects there is a "milestone" relationship (milestone projects). But "the milestone deadline of December 2, 2026" might refer to a milestone project linked to a project whose target date is December 2, 2026. Or it might refer to a project whose milestone field has a due date.

